---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Digital Training Solutions: VR & Digital Work Instructions"
  badge="Experience-based case study — anonymized"
  badgeType="anonymized"
  category="Digital Learning & VR"
  summary="Developing and rolling out immersive Virtual Reality simulations and interactive digital work instructions to transform shopfloor technical onboarding and complex assembly training."
  confidentialityNote="This case study describes technical training development methodologies, VR simulation workflows, and evaluation procedures. All specific equipment CAD assets, machine specifications, proprietary part numbers, and company metrics are excluded to uphold strict confidentiality."
  domains={["VR Training", "Digital Work Instructions", "Training Needs Analysis", "Effectiveness Evaluation"]}
>
  <h2>Context & Training Challenge</h2>
  <p>
    In precision manufacturing environments, onboarding operators and technicians to production machinery poses distinct challenges:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Physical machines cannot easily be halted for novice training without impacting active manufacturing output.</li>
    <li>Improper handling during live training creates safety risks and equipment calibration errors.</li>
    <li>Traditional static paper binders and printed procedures are difficult to digest quickly, lead to knowledge retention gaps, and lack interactive feedback.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To resolve these limitations, digital training solutions—including interactive Virtual Reality (VR) modules developed in Unity and structured digital work instructions—were introduced to create a safe, repeatable, and accessible learning environment.
  </p>

  <h2>Solution Lifecycle & Workflow</h2>
  <p>
    Developing effective technical training requires an instructional design lifecycle tailored to manufacturing discipline:
  </p>

  <div class="my-8 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white shadow-sm">
    <div class="bg-brand-cardmuted px-4 py-3 border-b border-brand-border">
      <h3 class="text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-slate m-0">Digital Training Solution Lifecycle</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-teal text-white text-xs font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center">01</span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy m-0">Training Needs Analysis (TNA)</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate mt-1 mb-0">Worked with line stakeholders to analyze recurring errors, safety considerations, and learning curves on production machinery.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-teal text-white text-xs font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center">02</span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy m-0">Instructional Objectives Definition</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate mt-1 mb-0">Deconstructed complex multi-step machine operations into clear, observable competency checkpoints and mandatory safety sequences.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-teal text-white text-xs font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center">03</span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy m-0">Solution Selection & Interaction Design</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate mt-1 mb-0">Determined appropriate medium: immersive 3D VR simulation for complex or high-consequence spatial procedures, and interactive digital work instructions for daily line reference.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-teal text-white text-xs font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center">04</span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy m-0">Content Development & Unity Integration</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate mt-1 mb-0">Modeled workflows, scripted interactive step verification in Unity, built visual cues, error state triggers, and intuitive digital instructional layouts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-teal text-white text-xs font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center">05</span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy m-0">Floor Implementation & Guided Rollout</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate mt-1 mb-0">Established dedicated training workstations, conducted facilitator orientations, and integrated digital modules into the standard technician onboarding curriculum.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-teal text-white text-xs font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center">06</span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy m-0">Effectiveness Evaluation</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate mt-1 mb-0">Gathered qualitative feedback from trainees and shift trainers, observing procedural confidence and identifying areas for module refinement.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Key Solution Components</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6 not-prose">
    <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-brand-teal uppercase mb-1">Immersive Media</div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy mb-1">Interactive VR Simulations (Unity)</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate">Allowed technicians to perform pre-operational safety inspections, virtual tool manipulation, and emergency shutdown drills in a zero-risk 3D environment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-brand-teal uppercase mb-1">Digital Standardization</div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy mb-1">Digital Work Instructions</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate">Replaced binder-based manuals with structured digital step-by-step guides featuring annotated images, critical callouts, and verification checkboxes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-brand-teal uppercase mb-1">Instructional Quality</div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy mb-1">Training Needs Analysis Templates</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate">Standardized matrix identifying skill gaps, task frequency, criticality levels, and appropriate training delivery formats across lines.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-white">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-brand-teal uppercase mb-1">Knowledge Transfer</div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-navy mb-1">Trainer Facilitation Playbooks</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-slate">Prepared structured debriefing prompts and evaluation checklists for trainers.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Reported Impact & Findings</h2>
  <div class="my-6 p-4 rounded-xl bg-teal-50/60 border border-teal-200">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-teal-900 m-0 mb-2">Qualitative Operational Impact</h3>
    <ul class="text-xs text-teal-950 space-y-1.5 mb-0">
      <li><strong>Reduced training time:</strong> Learners were able to familiarize themselves with machine interfaces and procedural workflows virtually before touching actual production machinery.</li>
      <li><strong>Improved accessibility:</strong> Training modules could be accessed on demand without waiting for scheduled machine downtime or supervisor availability.</li>
      <li><strong>Enhanced trainee confidence:</strong> Operators could repeat high-risk or complex sequences multiple times without fear of causing physical damage or production scrap.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="text-xs text-brand-muted italic">
    *Note: In accordance with professional integrity guidelines, only qualitative reported impacts are stated; no synthetic percentages, dollar savings, or unverified statistical KPIs are claimed.
  </p>
</CaseStudyLayout>
